# 2026-11-08 (r87, wall-85 fix): launchd died 68s after exec with
# OS_REASON_PAC_EXCEPTION (EXC_ARM_PAC_FAIL, key=DA) at the first userland
# AUTDA. The r86b capture line decodes against the 24A446 cache exactly: the
# fixup entry at unslid VA 0x1e8d37228 (.25.dylddata file 0x6c5b228) is
# auth=1 keyIsData=1(DA) addrDiv=1 diversity=0x9abf runtimeOffset=0x68d37270,
# and runtimeOffset + value_add (0x180000000) + slide (0x970000) = the
# captured x16 bit for bit - the kernel rebased the pointer but stored it
# UNSIGNED, so the consumer AUTDA can never pass. The unsigned store comes
# from the slide sign gate "jop_key != 0": launchd is a platform binary
# without a team id, so its shared_region_id is "" and
# shared_region_key_alloc("") takes ml_default_jop_pid(), which is 0 on
# non-paravirtualized (native PAC) hardware, so the gate skips signing for
# every auth fixup. Under HAS_NATIVE_PAC the kernel and all processes share
# one boot-derived key set (native-pac-keys.patch) and
# ml_enable_user_jop_key is a no-op, so the jop_key value is irrelevant to
# the signature; only its zero-ness gated signing at all. Sheng's bring-up
# patch deletes the jop_key != 0 term for exactly this reason, but that
# patch never made it into this lane (porting.toml bringup-merge-recon: it
# fails cross-file apply, series kept at the r52 baseline). This patch is
# the three gate hunks of zzzz-sheng-ipados27-bringup-core.patch verbatim,
# split out standalone; H-B (cache content / fixup metadata wrong) refuted
# by the entry decode, H-A (wrong DA key value) refuted by the 68s of
# passing IA/IB auth under the same shared key set.
arch:../../../patches/xnu-12377/sheng-shared-region-sign-gate.patch
